From: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Apr 2025 14:25:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: avoid WED 3.1 token-status false alarms

MT7987 WED 3.1 only enables RX_DRV_COHERENT in its external interrupt
mask.  The interrupt handler nevertheless classifies TKID_WO_PYLD as an
error for every WED v3-or-newer device.  That status bit can be latched
during normal PPE-to-WDMA Wi-Fi forwarding, producing a large number of
misleading "error status=00000002" messages even though the bit is not an
enabled WED 3.1 error interrupt.

Use the same WED 3.1 status mask when consuming and reporting the status
register.  Keep the existing WED v3 handling intact so this MT7987 fix does
not change diagnostics on other SoCs.

This is a narrow Linux 6.18 adaptation of MediaTek feed patch
999-wed-14-refactor-mtk_wed_irq_get-to-avoid-wed-status-false-a.patch.

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/671c2416d6219beb19abbb05709e418a6363be62/25.12/files/target/linux/mediatek/patches-6.12/999-wed-14-refactor-mtk_wed_irq_get-to-avoid-wed-status-false-a.patch
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
@@ -3012,7 +3012,9 @@ mtk_wed_irq_get(struct mtk_wed_device *d
 {
 	u32 val, ext_mask;
 
-	if (mtk_wed_is_v3_or_greater(dev->hw))
+	if (mtk_wed_is_v3_1(dev->hw))
+		ext_mask = MTK_WED_EXT_INT_STATUS_RX_DRV_COHERENT;
+	else if (mtk_wed_is_v3(dev->hw))
 		ext_mask = MTK_WED_EXT_INT_STATUS_RX_DRV_COHERENT |
 			   MTK_WED_EXT_INT_STATUS_TKID_WO_PYLD;
 	else
